# Build-context ignore for the repo-root Docker builds (apps/api, apps/web —
# both use `context: .`). Docker resolves .dockerignore from the context root,
# so this one file governs both. Keeps local secrets, VCS, caches, and installed
# dependencies out of the image layers (deps are reinstalled inside the build).
# Do NOT exclude apps/ or packages/ — the api image copies packages/ and the
# web image copies apps/web/; their lockfiles (uv.lock, pnpm-lock.yaml) are needed.
.git
.gitignore

# Env & secrets — never bake a local .env into a layer.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Python caches / virtualenvs
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/.venv
**/venv
**/.pytest_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/.mypy_cache
**/.coverage
**/htmlcov

# Node / Next
**/node_modules
**/.next
**/out
**/.turbo
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# Local databases and runtime artifacts
**/*.db
**/*.sqlite
**/storage
**/outbox
**/*.log
packages/silk_intel/silk_intel/data/cache
packages/silk_intel/silk_intel/data/traces

# The legacy silk_platform product must NEVER ship in a production image: it
# contains a cold-send queue with no per-email approval gate (ADR-0004). The
# api Dockerfile additionally fails the build if this reappears in the context.
packages/silk_intel/silk_intel/silk_platform

# Playwright / test output
**/playwright-report
**/test-results

# Terraform state / vars (never in an image)
**/.terraform
**/*.tfstate
**/*.tfstate.*
**/*.tfvars
**/*.tfvars.json

# OS
.DS_Store
